### Underload Demo (CMK)
<hr style="width:100%;border-bottom:3px solid black;">

The second flavor uses `compose.mk` as an **interpreter**, written in [CMK-lang]({{mkdocs.site_relative_url}}/compiler).  Besides the cleaner syntax, it shows off single-sourcing: rather than copy the shared pieces, it pulls the lexer in with [`mk.import.def`]({{mkdocs.site_relative_url}}/macros), the operator/stack targets with [`mk.import.target`]({{mkdocs.site_relative_url}}/macros), and the sample-program literals with `mk.import.def` -- all imported from the Makefile twin above, so the two stay in lock-step.

{{site.embed_demo('demos/cmk/underload.cmk',
    bottom_right=site.link_mirror(
